]]}],"hatch":[[[0.0,0.0],[0.0219,0.0],[0.0219,1.0],[0.0,1.0],[0.0,0.0]]],"settings":"$r_H = \\frac{1}{10}$, $\\theta = 0$, $\\varphi = 0$","input":"Herdeiro and Radu's configuration IV, in units of the field's inverse length $\\mu$: $r_H = 0.1/\\mu$, the field turns at $\\omega = 0.82\\,\\mu c$ with $m = 1$, and $GM/c^2 = 0.933/\\mu$ and $GJ/c^3 = 0.740/\\mu^2$, with $M$ the mass and $J$ the angular momentum. The four functions are those of the authors' numerical solution, interpolated between its grid points.","caption":["The plane of $t$ and $r$ on the axis ($\\theta = 0$, $\\varphi = 0$) of Herdeiro and Radu's configuration IV. On the axis the dragging drops out of the metric, which is $-e^{2F_0}(1 - r_H/r)c^2dt^2 + e^{2F_1}dr^2/(1 - r_H/r)$, and a ray has $c\\,dt/dr = \\pm e^{F_1 - F_0}/(1 - r_H/r)$; every rotation about the axis fixes the plane, so the rays are null geodesics.","The field vanishes on the axis. The cones close toward the horizon $r = r_H$, which a ray reaches only as $t \\to \\pm\\infty$, and where $e^{F_1 - F_0} = 31.2$. A ray climbs from $r = 0.2/\\mu$ to $4/\\mu$ in $11.6/\\mu$ of the time $ct$, and a clock at rest at $r = 0.2/\\mu$ runs at $0.197$ of the rate of one far away."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"861010e4ac7023f1"}},{"id":"equator","label":"$t$ and $r$ on the equator","plane":["t","r"],"families":["ingoing","outgoing"],"xlabel":"$\\mu r$","ylabel":"$\\mu ct$","ticks":{"x":[{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":2.0,"label":"$2$"},{"at":3.0,"label":"$3$"},{"at":4.0,"label":"$4$"}],"y":[{"at":-2.0,"label":"$-2$"},{"at":-1.0,"label":"$-1$"},{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":2.0,"label":"$2$"}]},"box":[0,4,-2,2],"to_display":[[0.0,1.0],[1.0,0.0]],"mirror":false,"rays":{"P":[[[0.0336,-0.0215],[0.0295,0.426],[0.027,1.021]],[[0.1029,-0.0213],[0.0899,0.0854],[0.0787,0.1948],[0.069,0.3094],[0.0607,0.4291],[